<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simhavishnu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 575–600</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Avanisimha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simhavishnu was a king of the Pallava dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late 6th century. He expelled the Kalabhras from the Kaveri delta, taking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> country, and with it the Pallavas became the leading power of the Tamil lands. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahendravarman-i">Mahendravarman I</a> continued the rise of the dynasty and began its rock-cut temples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simhavishnu.jpg" alt="Simhavishnu" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simhavishnu_portrait_in_stone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
